22.8. How Does synchronized Achieve Mutual Exclusion?

When a thread enters

synchronized(lock){

}

the JVM

Acquires the monitor.
Marks it as owned.
Blocks every other thread trying to acquire the same monitor.
Releases the monitor when leaving the synchronized block.

Only one owner exists at any point.
